# Large Repository Strategy

- Begin at module, owner, manifest, entrypoint, and public-contract boundaries.
- Search before reading broad trees; exclude generated and vendored content.
- Build a compact evidence map of paths, symbols, dependency edges, tests, and open questions.
- Inspect the complete diff and verify the affected module first.
- Expand to direct dependents, contract tests, integrations, or repository-wide checks according to evidence and risk.
- Parallelize independent reads. Serialize writes unless the task assigns explicit disjoint ownership and an integration owner.
- Treat shared manifests, lockfiles, generated output, and migrations as overlapping write ownership.
